Package: robart
Title: Bayesian Additive Regression Trees with Tree-Specific Rotations
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jeongung", "Heo", email = "jwheo@yonsei.ac.kr",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Robert", "McCulloch", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Original BART implementation"),
    person("Rodney", "Sparapani", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Original BART implementation"),
    person("Robert", "Gramacy", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Inherited BART latent-variable routines"),
    person("Charles", "Spanbauer", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Inherited BART native routines"))
Description: Fits Bayesian additive regression trees with tree-specific
    orthogonal rotations, centered angle proposals and joint cutpoint retuning.
    Provides Gaussian and Bernoulli-probit convenience interfaces and a common
    interface with a finite-mixture Bernoulli-logit implementation. Includes
    posterior draws, diagnostics and versioned state snapshots. The implementation
    builds on 'BART' as described by Sparapani, Spanbauer and McCulloch (2021)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v097.i01>. Prediction for rotated fits currently uses inputs
    supplied during fitting; arbitrary new-data prediction is not provided.
